## Summary

**Task 5.1/5.2 Complete: Integrate KaTeX for Math Formula Rendering**

I successfully integrated KaTeX for rendering LaTeX math formulas in the blog:

**Dependencies Added:**
- `katex@0.16.11` - LaTeX math rendering library
- `react-katex@3.0.1` - React component wrapper
- `@types/katex@0.16.7` - TypeScript definitions
- `remark-math@6.0.0` - Remark plugin for parsing math syntax
- `rehype-katex@7.0.1` - Rehype plugin for rendering KaTeX

**Files Created:**
- `components/math-block.tsx` - MathBlock component for KaTeX rendering
- `posts/2026-01-17-math-formula-test.md` - Test article with various math formulas

**Files Modified:**
- `components/mdx-content.tsx` - Added remark-math and rehype-katex plugins

**Features:**
- Inline math support using `$...$` syntax
- Block math support using `$$...$$` syntax
- Full LaTeX math syntax support via KaTeX
- Math formulas render server-side at build time (static HTML)
- Support for complex formulas (integrals, matrices, Fourier transforms, etc.)

**Build Status:** Verified successfully

